From c84e9cdab812841a6fba4cfc3ef49de10a2ca2dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chao Chen <209239467+surlymochan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:48:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(auth-api): refuse two account migrations with the same
 number

Wrangler applies apps/auth-api/migrations in name order and records each
applied name. Two pull requests that each add the next number pass review on
their own; after both merge, the order of the pair depends on the rest of the
file name, and the one that merges second may run before a migration it
depends on. 0034 already has two files for this reason.

- apps/auth-api/scripts/migration-numbers.ts refuses a reused number and a
  name that is not NNNN_lowercase_name.sql. Gaps stay allowed. The applied
  0034 pair stays allowed by name, so a third 0034 is refused.
- scripts/auth-migration-numbers-smoke.ts (bun run
  test:api-migration-numbers) checks the repository migrations and the rules,
  and writes .openbot-build/auth-migration-numbers.json.

No migration is renamed or changed, and CI is not changed.
